WEBVTT

1
00:00:15.462 --> 00:00:19.643
While Scrooge worked inside his office, the day darkened into night.

2
00:00:21.944 --> 00:00:24.985
Outside, the weather grew foggy and damp.

3
00:00:26.326 --> 00:00:30.888
The air temperature dropped even lower, making people shiver in their winter coats.

4
00:00:33.120 --> 00:00:35.761
Finally the end of the business day arrived.

5
00:00:37.581 --> 00:00:42.423
As soon as Bob Cratchit saw his boss rise from his stool, he leaped to his feet too.

6
00:00:44.263 --> 00:00:46.724
He put out his candle and reached for his hat.

7
00:00:49.825 --> 00:00:52.045
Scrooge stared coldly at his employee.

8
00:00:52.065 --> 00:00:57.787
"You'll want the whole day off tomorrow for Christmas, I suppose?"

9
00:00:58.347 --> 00:01:00.067
he asked in a disagreeable voice.

10
00:01:03.760 --> 00:01:05.541
"Yes." Cratchit smiled uncertainly.

11
00:01:05.561 --> 00:01:08.903
"Um, that is, if you don't mind, sir."

12
00:01:08.923 --> 00:01:12.045
"I do mind!"

13
00:01:12.485 --> 00:01:13.246
Scrooge said.

14
00:01:13.266 --> 00:01:17.788
"And not only that, but I also find it quite unfair.

15
00:01:20.230 --> 00:01:24.092
If I held back your pay, people would say you were poorly treated.

16
00:01:25.193 --> 00:01:30.556
Meanwhile nobody would consider me poorly treated if I paid you for no work!"

17
00:01:33.184 --> 00:01:35.565
"Christmas comes only once per year, Mr.

18
00:01:35.625 --> 00:01:37.746
Scrooge," Cratchit said softly.

19
00:01:39.507 --> 00:01:40.727
Scrooge let out a harrumph.

20
00:01:40.747 --> 00:01:46.950
"That's a poor excuse for picking a man's pocket every twenty-fifth of December.

21
00:01:48.470 --> 00:01:51.292
But I suppose you may have the day off.

22
00:01:52.652 --> 00:01:55.093
Make sure you're early on the following day!"

23
00:01:56.974 --> 00:01:58.315
Cratchit's eyes lit up.

24
00:01:58.335 --> 00:02:01.316
"I will be here early, sir!

25
00:02:02.620 --> 00:02:03.320
I promise!

26
00:02:03.700 --> 00:02:04.200
Thank you!"

27
00:02:07.241 --> 00:02:11.182
The two men shut up the office, and then Cratchit ran off down the street.

28
00:02:13.223 --> 00:02:18.504
Scrooge, however, walked slowly, ignoring all signs of the holiday around him.

29
00:02:22.065 --> 00:02:28.167
He ate his melancholy dinner in his usual melancholy inn, with only a newspaper for company.

30
00:02:31.268 --> 00:02:36.513
Then he walked home toward his apartment, which had once belonged to Jacob Marley.

31
00:02:37.714 --> 00:02:41.815
At the front door of the apartment building, Scrooge put his key in the lock.

32
00:02:43.695 --> 00:02:46.216
Then he blinked, startled by something odd.

33
00:02:46.236 --> 00:02:51.777
"Why does the door knocker look so strange?"

34
00:02:52.157 --> 00:02:52.658
he thought.

35
00:02:52.678 --> 00:02:54.998
"Is it the fog?"

36
00:02:57.259 --> 00:02:59.599
Scrooge leaned in closer for a better look.

37
00:03:01.860 --> 00:03:03.601
"M-Marley?" he gasped.

38
00:03:04.982 --> 00:03:09.366
To his shock, the door knocker had taken on the shape of his old partner's face.

39
00:03:10.907 --> 00:03:15.310
Marley looked much like himself, with his spectacles resting on his forehead.

40
00:03:16.331 --> 00:03:21.614
Yet his face was glowing with an eerie light, and an invisible breeze was stirring his hair.

41
00:03:23.976 --> 00:03:29.040
Suddenly the knocker seemed to freeze, returning to its usual appearance.

42
00:03:31.556 --> 00:03:34.279
Scrooge shook his head and muttered to himself.

43
00:03:35.860 --> 00:03:39.523
He was not usually frightened by things looking odd in the dark.

44
00:03:41.645 --> 00:03:46.850
Still, he couldn't help feeling uneasy as he unlocked the door and entered the building.

45
00:03:51.074 --> 00:03:54.196
He hurried toward the stairs, which were hidden in darkness.

46
00:03:55.658 --> 00:03:57.960
No one else lived in the rundown building.

47
00:03:58.944 --> 00:04:02.387
So there was no reason for Scrooge to expect to see anything there.

48
00:04:03.968 --> 00:04:07.791
However, tonight he saw something moving on the stairs.

49
00:04:09.432 --> 00:04:12.835
Horses were pulling a hearse and galloping up the steps ahead of him!

50
00:04:16.698 --> 00:04:19.300
Scrooge groaned and closed his eyes for a moment.

51
00:04:25.365 --> 00:04:28.588
must have eaten some bad meat at dinner," he thought.

52
00:04:29.568 --> 00:04:33.010
"The inn will hear my complaint tomorrow, Christmas or not!"

53
00:04:35.832 --> 00:04:38.193
He stomped up the stairs and into his apartment.

54
00:04:40.054 --> 00:04:42.055
Once again he felt oddly worried.

55
00:04:44.336 --> 00:04:46.778
He checked each room to be sure he was alone.

56
00:04:47.818 --> 00:04:52.641
To his relief, there was nobody behind the sitting room sofa or under the bed.

57
00:04:56.103 --> 00:04:58.024
All the closets looked just as they should.

58
00:05:00.204 --> 00:05:03.227
Finally satisfied, he locked the door behind him.

59
00:05:06.390 --> 00:05:11.715
He changed into his slippers and bathrobe, and sat down near the fire with a cup of tea.

60
00:05:13.376 --> 00:05:15.278
Dong! Dong!

61
00:05:16.439 --> 00:05:19.462
He nearly dropped the cup when a bell rang out from behind him.

62
00:05:20.983 --> 00:05:25.568
Spinning around, he saw that the bell hanging in the corner was swinging back and forth.

63
00:05:28.328 --> 00:05:33.151
Back when the building had been one large house, the bell had been used to summon servants.

64
00:05:35.072 --> 00:05:39.174
But since Scrooge had no use for it, he had never heard it ring before.

65
00:05:41.235 --> 00:05:43.156
Suddenly more bells began to ring.

66
00:05:46.878 --> 00:05:48.839
Scrooge felt a terrible dread.

67
00:05:50.040 --> 00:05:53.622
"First the door knocker, then the stairs, and now this.

68
00:05:54.822 --> 00:05:56.583
What on earth is going on?"

69
00:05:56.944 --> 00:05:57.364
he thought.

70
00:05:59.152 --> 00:06:01.093
All at once the bells stopped.

71
00:06:03.614 --> 00:06:06.836
Then a loud clanking noise rose from somewhere below.

72
00:06:06.856 --> 00:06:13.179
It sounded as if someone was dragging heavy chains across the floor and up the stairs.

73
00:06:13.199 --> 00:06:16.400
"What's that awful sound?"

74
00:06:17.000 --> 00:06:18.021
Scrooge whispered.

75
00:06:19.181 --> 00:06:21.182
The clanking sound came closer.

76
00:06:23.063 --> 00:06:24.664
Soon it was right outside his door.

77
00:06:26.100 --> 00:06:28.962
Then a dark figure slipped into the room.

78
00:06:30.664 --> 00:06:36.048
As the fire crackled and flamed higher, Scrooge could finally see his frightening visitor.

79
00:06:36.068 --> 00:06:39.230
"I know you!"

80
00:06:40.251 --> 00:06:43.053
Scrooge cried, dropping to the floor in shock.

81
00:06:43.073 --> 00:06:46.776
"You're Jacob Marley!"
